    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. but what about when the city inspector is being really difficult about the \"encroachment\" part? like, if they're treating a tiny structural overlap like it's a massive violation of the boundary. is there any specific legal precedent or administrative way to frame that \"intrusion\" so it doesn't kill the whole reclassification process?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
