      "content": "You can often frame this by classifying the overlap as a \"de minimis\" issue, arguing that the encroachment is too minor to constitute a实质性的 (substantial) violation under state law. Administratively, request a variance request focused specifically on the encroachment to create a record showing the council weighed non-safety factors differently than the distance requirements. Additionally, requesting an administrative appeal or hearing allows for formal submission of engineering reports proving the intrusion ignores safe boundary lines without compromising structural integrity.",
