      "content": "thanks. one more thing—the inspector keeps using the word \"trespass\" when describing how the foundation sits on the line. it's making the whole thing feel like a much bigger deal than a simple setback error. if they start pushing the idea that this \"unauthorized presence\" on the property line is a fundamental breach of the land use, how do i pivot the conversation back to the technical zoning requirements instead of getting bogged down in the \"trespassing\" semantics?",
